&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a meticulous, proactive, and collaborative teammate to join our Renewals team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an &lt;strong&gt;Associate Account Manager, Revenue Retention&lt;/strong&gt; in JFrog you will be a key driver of the “Liquid Software” vision by ensuring our customers&#39; journey with JFrog remains seamless and uninterrupted. By mastering the renewals lifecycle, you enable the world&#39;s leading organizations to maintain their continuous delivery pipelines with confidence and speed. Your technical precision in account management ensures that the flow of innovation never stops, making you a vital architect of our customer retention and long-term success.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;As an Associate Account Manager, Revenue Retention, in JFrog you will...&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scale the renewals process by architecting accurate quotes and opportunities across a targeted global portfolio.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive operational excellence by collaborating with Finance, Legal, and Deal Desk to ensure 100% contract accuracy and compliance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maximize customer retention by proactively managing the end-to-end renewal lifecycle within your assigned territory, including tracking pending signatures through to close and understanding the downstream consequences of a lapsed renewal (especially on usage-based and cloud products) well enough to create urgency with the customer without being prompted.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Optimize Salesforce data integrity to provide real-time visibility into renewal health and territory performance, recognizing that clean, current data is the direct input to the AI-driven renewal risk scoring this team runs on.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Accelerate business growth by identifying expansion opportunities and providing actionable insights during the renewal cycle using AI-assisted signal review (Gong call analysis, renewal risk scoring) to surface expansion opportunities before they show up in a standard pipeline review.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recognize strategic deal signals and streamline the customer experience by orchestrating high-touch communications and owning contract and legal-adjacent processes end-to-end.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Approach the renewal motion as something actively evolving with AI-assisted tooling, ready to take on higher-complexity, higher-touch accounts as routine tiers become more automated.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;To be an Associate Account Manager, Revenue Retention&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;in JFrog you need...&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A minimum of 4 years of relevant experience in account management, renewals, or sales operations within a SaaS environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of managing high-volume portfolios and meeting tight deadlines with exceptional attention to detail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced proficiency in Salesforce (SFDC) and the MS Office Suite, particularly Excel, including working deal math independently: discount deltas, co-term pricing across tiers, and monthly-vs-annual savings comparisons.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated problem-solving skills with the ability to navigate complex internal processes and cross-functional dependencies, including contract and legal workflow literacy (JSA, DPA, NDA, compliance routing).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong verbal and written communication skills to effectively engage with both internal stakeholders and external customer liaisons.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a fast-paced, high-growth technical environment where adaptability and a “Froggy” spirit are essential, with working depth on the JFrog platform itself (Xray, edge nodes, tiering) enough to handle a technical objection without a one-line script.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI fluency for non-technical, customer-facing work: using AI to accelerate research and drafting, then verifying the output before treating it as finished.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT JFROG CAN OFFER…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At JFrog, base salary is only one component of our compensation package.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This position has a base salary range between $90,000 to $115,000. &amp;nbsp;Base salary will be based on your skills, qualifications, experience and location.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Additionally, this role may be eligible for discretionary bonuses or commission payments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This position also includes an equity package of restricted stock units (RSU). &amp;nbsp;In addition, JFrog employees are eligible to participate in our Employee Stock Purchase Plan.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;JFrog provides employees comprehensive benefits including medical, dental, vision, retirement, wellness and much more!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;JFrog embraces hybrid work: 3 days in office / 2 days remote.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
